GOG Import
==========

Gets the files VCMI needs (Data, Maps and Mp3) out of the GOG.com
installer of Heroes of Might and Magic III Complete, on RISC OS, so
you don't need Windows, Linux or a Mac to set up VCMI.

You need the game's GOG installer, both parts, in the same directory:

  setup_heroes_of_might_and_magic_3_complete_4.0_(...)_gog_..._(nnnnn).exe
  setup_heroes_of_might_and_magic_3_complete_4.0_(...)_gog_..._(nnnnn)-1.bin

(GOG.com, "Heroes of Might and Magic 3: Complete", offline backup game
installer.) About 1 GB of free disc space is needed for the files.

How to use it
-------------
1. Double-click !GOGImport. Its icon appears on the icon bar.
2. Drag the installer (the .exe, or the -1.bin) onto that icon, or into
   the window it opens.
3. The files go into !VCMI.H3data if the Filer has seen !VCMI (open the
   directory !VCMI is in first). To choose another place, drag !VCMI or
   a directory into the window.
4. Click Import. It takes a few minutes; the window shows each file as
   it's unpacked. When it's finished, double-click !VCMI to play.

You can also drag the installer straight onto !GOGImport in a Filer
window.

How it works
------------
It runs innoextract 1.9 (Daniel Scharrer's Inno Setup unpacker,
https://constexpr.org/innoextract/) in a TaskWindow, so the desktop keeps
running. innoextract can be used on its own from the command line too:
*<GOGImport$Dir>.innoextract --help

This is part of the RISC OS port of VCMI:
https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-vcmi

